<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nanjaraja</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nanjarajaiah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nanjaraja was an eighteenth-century minister of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> from the Kalale family. With his elder brother, the dalavayi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devaraja">Devaraja</a>, he dominated the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnaraja-wodeyar-ii">Krishnaraja Wodeyar II</a> from the 1730s, holding the office of sarvadhikari, and he drew Mysore into the wars of the Carnatic around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiruchirappalli">Tiruchirappalli</a> in the 1750s. The soldier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> rose in his service and pushed the brothers aside by 1761.</p></div>
